{"tool_name":"spoton","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"spoton","home":"https://alcazar.science.uu.nl/cgi/services/SPOTON/spoton/","summary":"Determination of Hot-Spots at protein-protein interfaces\n\nSpotOn is a robust algorithm developed to identify and classify the interfacial residues as Hot-Spots (HS) and Null-Spots (NS) with a final accuracy of 0.95 and a sensitivity of 0.95 on an independent test set.","addition_date":"2018-10-02T12:00:13Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:23:06.556212Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"collections":["BioExcel","EGI","EOSC-Hub","INSTRUCT","West-Life"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:spoton","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"a.m.j.j.bonvin@uu.nl","name":"Bonvin Lab","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7369-1322","typeEntity":"Division","typeRole":["Developer","Maintainer","Primary contact","Provider"],"url":"http://www.bonvinlab.org"},{"name":"European H2020 e-Infrastructure grant, BioExcel, grant no. 675728"},{"name":"European H2020 e-Infrastructure grant, BioExcel, grant no. 823830"},{"name":"European H2020 e-Infrastructure grant, West-Life VRE, grant no. 675858"},{"name":"Netherlands Organization for Scientific Research (NWO) , TOP-PUNT grant no. 718.015.001"},{"name":"EGI","url":"https://www.egi.eu"},{"name":"Utrecht University","url":"https://www.uu.nl"}],"documentation":[{"note":"Support forum","type":["Other"],"url":"https://ask.bioexcel.eu/c/spoton"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://milou.science.uu.nl/cgi/services/SPOTON/spoton/help"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["a.m.j.j.bonvin@uu.nl"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Protein structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1460"},"format":[{"term":"Format (by type of data)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2350"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Prediction and recognition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2423"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"SpotOn","owner":"a.m.j.j.bonvin@uu.nl","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-017-08321-2","metadata":{"abstract":"We present SpotOn, a web server to identify and classify interfacial residues as Hot-Spots (HS) and Null-Spots (NS). SpotON implements a robust algorithm with a demonstrated accuracy of 0.95 and sensitivity of 0.98 on an independent test set. The predictor was developed using an ensemble machine learning approach with up-sampling of the minor class. It was trained on 53 complexes using various features, based on both protein 3D structure and sequence. The SpotOn web interface is freely available at: http://milou.science.uu.nl/services/SPOTON/.","authors":[{"name":"Almeida J.G."},{"name":"Bonvin A.M.J.J."},{"name":"Costa J."},{"name":"Gumus Z.H."},{"name":"Koukos P.I."},{"name":"Melo R."},{"name":"Moreira I.S."},{"name":"Preto A.J."},{"name":"Schaarschmidt J."},{"name":"Trellet M."}],"citationCount":74,"date":"2017-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Scientific Reports","title":"SpotOn: High Accuracy Identification of Protein-Protein Interface Hot-Spots"},"pmcid":"PMC5556074","pmid":"28808256","type":["Primary"]},{"doi":"10.3390/ijms17081215","metadata":{"abstract":"Understanding protein-protein interactions is a key challenge in biochemistry. In this work, we describe a more accurate methodology to predict Hot-Spots (HS) in protein-protein interfaces from their native complex structure compared to previous published Machine Learning (ML) techniques. Our model is trained on a large number of complexes and on a significantly larger number of different structural- and evolutionary sequence-based features. In particular, we added interface size, type of interaction between residues at the interface of the complex, number of different types of residues at the interface and the Position-Specific Scoring Matrix (PSSM), for a total of 79 features. We used twenty-seven algorithms from a simple linear-based function to support-vector machine models with different cost functions. The best model was achieved by the use of the conditional inference random forest (c-forest) algorithm with a dataset pre-processed by the normalization of features and with up-sampling of the minor class. The method has an overall accuracy of 0.80, an F1-score of 0.73, a sensitivity of 0.76 and a specificity of 0.82 for the independent test set.","authors":[{"name":"Bonvin A.M.J.J."},{"name":"Cordeiro M.N.D.S."},{"name":"Correia J.D.G."},{"name":"Costa J."},{"name":"Fieldhouse R."},{"name":"Gumus Z.H."},{"name":"Melo A."},{"name":"Melo R."},{"name":"Moreira I.S."}],"citationCount":45,"date":"2016-08-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"International Journal of Molecular Sciences","title":"A machine learning approach for hot-spot detection at protein-protein interfaces"},"pmcid":"PMC5000613","pmid":"27472327","type":["Method"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Computational biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3307"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"SpotOn","home":"https://bio.tools/spoton","summary":"Determination of Hot-Spots at protein-protein interfaces\n\nSpotOn is a robust algorithm developed to identify and classify the interfacial residues as Hot-Spots (HS) and Null-Spots (NS) with a final accuracy of 0.95 and a sensitivity of 0.95 on an independent test set.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:spoton/web/alcazar.science.uu.nl","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":23,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"-1"},{"count":1,"year":"2020"},{"count":1,"year":"2023"},{"count":1,"year":"2024"},{"count":2,"year":"2016"},{"count":2,"year":"2017"},{"count":2,"year":"2022"},{"count":3,"year":"2018"},{"count":3,"year":"2019"},{"count":3,"year":"2025"},{"count":4,"year":"2021"}],"doi":"10.3390/ijms17081215","pmcid":"PMC500061